.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-capture-show 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-capture\-show \- Print a capture\*(Aqs pointer, or the lines a selection asks for, with no second run
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten capture show\fR [\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-grep\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-J\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIhandle\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print a capture\*(Aqs pointer, or the lines a selection asks for, with no second run
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lines\fR
A 1\-indexed inclusive line range, `FROM:TO`, clamped to the capture
.TP
\fB\-\-grep\fR
Only lines containing this literal substring
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Write the selected bytes to stdout verbatim, with no decode and no added newline
.TP
\fB\-\-bytes\fR
A 0\-indexed half\-open byte range, `FROM:TO`, either side omittable, clamped to the capture
.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit byte\-stable JSON instead of pointer lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIhandle\fR>
The `<stream>:<digest>` handle to read
